  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "10. Shooting Phase",
    "ruleNumber": "10.07",
    "summary": "An [Unengaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) unit can select this mode if it has an **[[INDIRECT FIRE]](vsdata:weapon-ability/indirect-fire)** weapon and has made no [Advance move](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) this turn. Resolve the attacks using [Making Attacks](vsdata:core-rule/making-attacks). The unit's **[[INDIRECT FIRE]](vsdata:weapon-ability/indirect-fire)** weapons can pick targets their firers cannot see, and those targets receive the [Benefit of Cover](vsdata:core-rule/benefit-of-cover). Hit rolls cannot be rerolled, and unmodified 1–5 miss. Use 1–3 instead if a friendly unit sees the target and the firing unit [Remained Stationary](vsdata:core-rule/remain-stationary) this turn. The unit loses eligibility for the rest of the phase after shooting.",
